WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:04.840
Bad Boys for Life is full of bullets, explosions,
and quips, but is it any good?

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:06.620
That depends what you're looking for.

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:10.320
Here are our picks for the five best -- and
five worst -- things in this long-dormant

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:12.920
action franchise's latest installment.

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:18.060
It's been more than 15 years since they last
teamed up, but Will Smith and Martin Lawrence

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:18.880
haven't lost a step.

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:23.380
By this point in their careers, both actors
have their shticks down pat, and in Bad Boys

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:26.890
for Life they deploy their respective charms
with military precision.

00:00:26.890 --> 00:00:30.759
The action scenes are nice to look at, but
the banter between the two leads is where

00:00:30.759 --> 00:00:32.210
you'll find the real fireworks.

00:00:32.210 --> 00:00:34.160
"Hands behind your head, right now."

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:37.020
"I got this — I'mma penetrate this man's
soul with my heart."

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:40.760
When the script is clunky and the dialogue
cliched, Smith and Lawrence still make it

00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:41.300
work.

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:45.380
In a different world, Smith and Lawrence would've
been a modern Bob Hope and Bing Crosby.

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:48.100
Since that didn't happen, we'll take whatever
we can get.

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:54.040
Not all Bad Boys are created equal, and Bad
Boys for Life proves it: This is Mike Lowrey's

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:54.560
movie.

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:57.860
He's the one who's targeted by the bad guys,
he's the one who has the biggest character

00:00:57.860 --> 00:01:00.540
arc, and he's the one who drives the action
forward.

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:04.920
Unfortunately, that makes Martin Lawrence
more of a sidekick than an equal player.

00:01:05.260 --> 00:01:09.880
In the first Bad Boys, Marcus is very funny,
but he's also depicted as a capable cop and

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:10.920
legitimate tough guy.

00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:13.880
In Bad Boys for Life, he's little more than
comedic relief.

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:18.500
While Mike is out busting heads and chasing
leads, Marcus is stuck at home, engaging in

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:19.900
sitcom-style slapstick.

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:22.560
We get it, of course: Will Smith is the bigger
star.

00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:26.960
But Bad Boys is supposed to be a partnership,
and in the series' third installment, Smith

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:28.180
is clearly the star of the show.

00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:30.920
"Yo, day one, Miami Beach, son.

00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:33.380
Little Mike Lowery got me tearing up about
this thing."

00:01:34.510 --> 00:01:37.080
The first Bad Boys came out 25 years ago.

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:38.720
Will Smith is now 51.

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:40.200
Martin Lawrence is 54.

00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:42.900
To pretend that they're both still young would
be ridiculous.

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:46.500
But Bad Boys for Life lets its actors show
their age — and it's a better movie for

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:47.040
it.

00:01:47.060 --> 00:01:50.520
Lowrey and Burnett are still cop caricatures,
but they feel more lived-in than ever before,

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:52.660
which helps to sell the drama.

00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:55.640
"It's probably the last year my knees will
work."

00:01:55.640 --> 00:01:56.380
"Ha."

00:01:56.380 --> 00:01:57.380
"Ha ha ha."

00:01:57.640 --> 00:02:02.140
The characters' ages also let Bad Boys for
Life tackle an inconvenient truth: Bad Boys

00:02:02.140 --> 00:02:03.850
hasn't aged particularly well.

00:02:03.850 --> 00:02:06.840
The older movies are homophobic and slightly
racist.

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:10.759
Lowrey and Burnett's shoot first, ask questions
later-style of policing is a little harder

00:02:10.759 --> 00:02:14.470
to swallow given recent conversations about
police brutality.

00:02:14.470 --> 00:02:17.719
Bad Boys for Life deals with those issues,
at least indirectly.

00:02:17.719 --> 00:02:21.310
It's still gleefully un-PC, with a fantastically
high body count.

00:02:21.310 --> 00:02:23.440
Still, a little self-awareness goes a long
way.

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:29.020
Bad Boys for Life succeeds because of its
cast, but its script does them very few favors.

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:33.620
Many of Smith and Lawrence's one-liners, especially
those in the first half of the movie, feel

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:34.160
stale.

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:38.000
We've seen a cop pulled out of retirement
for "one last job" so often that it's beyond

00:02:38.140 --> 00:02:38.700
a cliche.

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:43.200
Beyond some memorable villains and a couple
of plot twists, most of the story is forgettable.

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:45.050
The same goes for the action scenes.

00:02:45.050 --> 00:02:50.299
After 25 years, over the top, Michael Bay-esque
explosion-fests are starting to have diminishing

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:50.840
returns.

00:02:50.840 --> 00:02:54.600
The action gets the job done, but it's not
particularly exciting or interesting.

00:02:54.920 --> 00:02:59.040
This may be one of 2020's first movies, but
in a lot of ways, it's still stuck in the

00:02:59.040 --> 00:02:59.800
mid-90s.

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:04.260
Bad Boys for Life is the most personal Bad
Boys film yet.

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:07.959
Marcus has always been a family man, but the
one-two punch of a new grandkid and a fresh

00:03:07.959 --> 00:03:11.530
son-in-law make him think about hanging up
his gun and badge for good.

00:03:11.530 --> 00:03:15.239
Mike has it even worse: At the beginning of
the movie, he's gunned down in a surprise

00:03:15.239 --> 00:03:19.239
drive-by shooting by an old rival, setting
him on the road towards vengeance.

00:03:19.239 --> 00:03:23.610
The Bad Boys have always been fun to watch,
but in Bad Boys for Life, they're also relatable.

00:03:23.610 --> 00:03:27.239
For the first time, it feels like we're getting
a glimpse at what’s underneath their cool,

00:03:27.239 --> 00:03:28.569
wisecracking demeanors.

00:03:28.569 --> 00:03:32.400
The old "One last job" cliche never works
out well for the people involved, and it's

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:35.980
never clear whether Mike or Marcus are going
to survive until the credits roll.

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:38.720
There are real consequences for the characters
in this movie.

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:42.800
Compared to Bad Boys II, in which the boys
just up and decide to single-handedly invade

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:44.360
Cuba, that's kind of a miracle.

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:49.220
Bad Boys for Life raises interesting questions,
and doesn't really do anything with them,

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:53.960
from Marcus' solemn promise to be done with
violence to Mike's newfound sense of vulnerability,

00:03:53.960 --> 00:03:55.440
and the anger that comes with it.

00:03:55.720 --> 00:03:59.829
Both of those concepts suggest unique stories
for the characters, but these weighty themes

00:03:59.829 --> 00:04:02.780
generally end up either ignored, or just played
for laughs.

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:06.800
Lowrey's fury is simply used as an excuse
to get him involved with the investigation.

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:11.360
Burnett's attempts to keep from killing fuel
punchlines, not character arcs, and pay off

00:04:11.360 --> 00:04:13.880
with Marcus picking up a machine gun and kicking
ass.

00:04:14.180 --> 00:04:15.440
Now, this is Bad Boys.

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:17.220
It's supposed to be fun, not introspective.

00:04:17.560 --> 00:04:20.480
Still, it feels like a bit of perhaps wasted
potential.

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:25.760
Directors Adil El Arbi and Billal Fallah are
the first people not named Michael Bay to

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:30.180
direct a Bad Boys movie, but don't feel bad
if you haven't heard of them: Bad Boys for

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:32.580
Life is their first major American film.

00:04:32.820 --> 00:04:35.850
Arbi and Fallah capture Bay's style without
mimicking him completely.

00:04:35.850 --> 00:04:39.160
They don't move the camera as much, and they
give some of the bigger shots more room to

00:04:39.160 --> 00:04:39.700
breathe.

00:04:40.120 --> 00:04:43.420
By the time the movie's over, it feels clear
that some new blood behind the camera was

00:04:43.540 --> 00:04:45.440
exactly what the franchise needed.

00:04:46.480 --> 00:04:48.100
So, about that plot twist...

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:52.860
Without giving too much away, Bad Boys for
Life's third act kicks off with a major revelation.

00:04:52.860 --> 00:04:57.680
As it turns out, Isabel has a much more personal
reason for hunting Mike than the film initially

00:04:57.680 --> 00:04:58.220
lets on.

00:04:58.480 --> 00:05:01.280
Unfortunately, the big twist comes more or
less out of nowhere.

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:06.960
It's a secret so big that even Marcus Burnett
— Mike's best friend for over 25 years — doesn't

00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:07.500
know about it.

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:12.620
That doesn't really ring true, and unfortunately,
the reveal derails Bad Boys for Life's climax

00:05:12.620 --> 00:05:14.260
and sucks all the fun out of the room.

00:05:14.260 --> 00:05:17.860
Even worse, it needlessly complicates Mike
Lowrey’s origin story.

00:05:18.280 --> 00:05:22.660
Bad Boys establishes that Lowrey is a handsome,
privileged trust-fund kid who always dreamed

00:05:22.660 --> 00:05:23.700
about being a cop.

00:05:23.980 --> 00:05:28.450
He takes his job seriously, but he's also
entitled and not used to being told no.

00:05:28.450 --> 00:05:32.420
It's a great, simple backstory that explains
everything the character does perfectly.

00:05:32.420 --> 00:05:34.300
It didn't need to be any more complicated.

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:38.500
Bad Boys for Life isn't the sort of film that
you watch for callbacks, references, or Easter

00:05:38.500 --> 00:05:39.040
eggs.

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:42.320
And yet, somehow, it's full if nods to the
previous two films.

00:05:42.720 --> 00:05:45.970
Even better, these Easter eggs don't call
attention to themselves.

00:05:45.970 --> 00:05:50.300
They're fun for diehard Bad Boys fans, but
series newcomers will find them funny, too.

00:05:50.300 --> 00:05:51.460
And boy, are there a lot of 'em.

00:05:51.780 --> 00:05:55.960
Marcus' quip that the "Bad Boys" lyrics are
hard to learn is a throwback to Bad Boys 2,

00:05:55.960 --> 00:05:59.720
which reveals that he doesn't know the words
to his own self-appointed theme song, as is

00:05:59.720 --> 00:06:03.520
his reference to his one good butt cheek,
after Mike shot him in the rear in the last

00:06:03.580 --> 00:06:04.140
movie.

00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:08.000
And then, of course, there's Michael Bay himself
as the MC at Marcus' daughter's wedding, a

00:06:08.220 --> 00:06:10.980
cameo that's tailor-made for the film nerds
in the audience.

00:06:11.440 --> 00:06:13.300
Even the kids at AMMO get in on the action.

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:17.620
When Will Smith dismisses the young task force
as a bunch of High School Musical wannabes,

00:06:17.630 --> 00:06:22.110
it's not just a sly dig: his co-star, Vanessa
Hudgens, rose to fame as the lead of the Disney

00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:22.640
Channel series.

00:06:24.020 --> 00:06:27.110
Ending Bad Boys for Life on a cliffhanger
feels unnecessary.

00:06:27.110 --> 00:06:30.651
By the end of the film, Lowrey and Burnett
have gone through complete arcs, and they're

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:32.360
content with their places in the world.

00:06:32.970 --> 00:06:35.720
Dramatically, there's nowhere else for these
characters to go.

00:06:35.730 --> 00:06:39.620
But it looks like they're forging forward
anyway; as of mid-January, a fourth movie

00:06:39.620 --> 00:06:42.370
is already in the works, according to The
Hollywood Reporter.

00:06:42.600 --> 00:06:46.760
Reportedly, we won't have to wait as long
to see the Boys again as we did between 1

00:06:46.760 --> 00:06:50.300
&amp; 2, but one wonders if it wouldn't have been
smarter to just wrap this unlikely series

00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:52.460
up more tidily, and just go out on top.

00:06:52.710 --> 00:06:56.120
The Bad Boys are getting older, and it really
makes you wonder what they're going to do

00:06:56.120 --> 00:06:56.820
for the next one.

00:06:57.120 --> 00:07:00.060
At this rate, they're gonna have to start
calling them Bad Grandpas.

